{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1260,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Hear us, Shepherd of Israel, you who lead Joseph like a flock, you who sit above the cherubim, shine out.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4371},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1261,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"Before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh, stir up your might! Come to save us!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4375},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1262,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Turn us again, God. Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4378},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1263,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"LORD God of Armies, how long will you be angry against the prayer of your people?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4383},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1264,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"You have fed them with the bread of tears, and given them tears to drink in large measure.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4386},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1265,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"You make us a source of contention to our neighbors. Our enemies laugh among themselves.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4389},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1266,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Turn us again, God of Armies. Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4392},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1267,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"You brought a vine out of Egypt. You drove out the nations, and planted it.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4397},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1268,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"You cleared the ground for it. It took deep root, and filled the land.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4400},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1269,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"The mountains were covered with its shadow. Its boughs were like God’s cedars.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4403},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1270,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"It sent out its branches to the sea, its shoots to the River.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4406},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1271,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"Why have you broken down its walls, so that all those who pass by the way pluck it?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4409},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1272,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"The boar out of the wood ravages it. The wild animals of the field feed on it.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4412},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1273,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"Turn again, we beg you, God of Armies. Look down from heaven, and see, and visit this vine,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4415},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1274,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"the stock which your right hand planted, the branch that you made strong for yourself.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4418},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1275,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"It’s burned with fire. It’s cut down. They perish at your rebuke.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4421},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1276,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"Let your hand be on the man of your right hand, on the son of man whom you made strong for yourself.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4425},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1277,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"So we will not turn away from you. Revive us, and we will call on your name.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4428},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":80,"verse_ordinal":1278,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"Turn us again, LORD God of Armies. Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4431}]}